# Git and Collaboration

Work on a feature branch. Open a pull request. Do not commit directly to the shared branch.

## Focus

Change only the files the task needs. Do not reformat, rename, or refactor unrelated code in the same change.

Keep a pull request to one phase concern so another developer can review it quickly.

## Ownership

Developer 1 owns `frontend/`. Developer 2 owns API routes, services, repositories, scoring, and migrations. Developer 3 owns ingestion, AI, RAG, and the scheduler. Do not edit another owner's area without saying so first.

Integrate through `docs/API_CONTRACT.md` and `docs/DATABASE_DESIGN.md`, not by reading each other's private helpers.

## Secrets

Do not commit `.env`, API keys, Clerk secrets, or SAM.gov keys. Example files contain placeholders only.

## Architecture notes

If a change alters a boundary, a table, or an endpoint, update the owning document in the same change after the conflict protocol allows it. Do not leave the decision only in the code.
